   "part": 1,
   "pin": null,
   "question": "",
   "quote": "would it be safer to wrap the assertions in a `try...finally` block so that the block file is always restored, even if an assertion or unexpected exception causes the test to exit early.",
   "request": "Wrap functional test assertions in a try...finally block so the renamed block file is always restored",
   "status": "answered",
   "status_by": {
    "at": "2026-09-23",
    "by": "maflcko",
    "id": "rc:4084843804",
    "quote": "I don\u2019t think a finally block is needed here: if an assertion fails, the functional test\u2019s temporary datadir is deleted "
   },
   "status_note": "maflcko explained teardown deletes the temporary test directory anyway so restoring the file is unnecessary",
   "type": "suggestion",
